@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+---
+name: gemm-f16-progress
+description: Running TFLOPS log + bottleneck analysis for the A100 fp16 GEMM kernel optimization task
+metadata:
+  type: project
+---
+
+A100 fp16 GEMM (task-1), pushing toward 312 TFLOPS peak. Scored via `./task1.sh run --float f16 --ver N` (100-round avg, 4096³). All versions use mma.sync.m16n8k16 + fp32 accum (error ~3e-5). A100 = sm_80, pinned in cmake/compilers/cuda-compiler-configs.cmake.
+
+**Version log (task1 100-round scoring):**
+- v1 WMMA baseline: 29.9 TFLOPS
+- v2 mma+cp.async double-buffer, block128x128 BK32, warp64x32: 48 TFLOPS (218M bank conflicts!)
+- v3 = v2 + smem pad (AP=8, ldm 40/136): 96.3 TFLOPS (0 conflicts; key fix: pad makes 8-row ldmatrix matrices hit 8 distinct bank groups)
+- v4 = v3 + 4-stage cp.async pipeline (dynamic smem): 133.7 TFLOPS (tensor util 56%, occ 24% = 2 blk/SM, 126 reg, DRAM 17%)
+
+**Recipe that works (verified correct):** A,B stored row-major in smem (cp.async-friendly), A via ldmatrix.x4, B via ldmatrix.x2.trans. mma m16n8k16.row.col.f32.f16.f16.f32 with "+f" accumulators. Store: thread holds 4 fp32 per 16x8 tile, row=base+lane/4 (and +8), col=base+(lane%4)*2 (and +1).
+
+- v5 (mainloop restructure: single sync + prefetch-BEFORE-compute + inner double-buf): 103 — REGRESSED. Prefetch-before-compute clogs MIO before ldmatrix. Don't move global prefetch before compute.
+- v6 (warp 64x64, block 128x256): 114 — REGRESSED (1 blk/SM, occupancy loss > intensity gain)
+- v7 (v4 + ldmatrix.x4.trans for B + single sync): 130 — flat vs v4
+- v8 configurable sweep (10 configs). Plateau 95-133. Best CFG3 256x128x32 warp64x64 = 133. CFG0=130, CFG2 BK64=129. **Whole family caps ~133 = 43% peak.**
+
+**KEY GOTCHA:** loader `for(v=tid;v<VA;v+=NT)` has tid-dependent trip count -> NOT unrolled -> 130->95 regression. ALWAYS use `for(i=0;i<VA/NT;++i){v=tid+i*NT;}` (compile-time trip count).
+
+**Diagnosis at 133:** stalls = mio_throttle 3.95 (ldmatrix burst), math_pipe 3.49, barrier 2.61, wait 2.24. No-eligible-warp 77%, occ capped 2 blk/SM by 64+ accum regs. Ceiling is MAINLOOP STRUCTURE: serial ldmatrix-burst -> mma-burst -> sync, MIO & tensor pipes never overlap.
+
+- v9 interleaved inner-K mainloop (ldmatrix(ki+1) overlaps mma(ki), global prefetch issued at last ki). Configurable sweep. **Interleaving crushed mio_throttle 3.95->0.49.**
+  - Best = CFG11 {BM256,BN128,BK64,WMc4,WNc2,3stage} = warp 64x64, 8 warps, 1 blk/SM, **158.4 TFLOPS, tensor util 66.9%, 220 reg.**
+  - Sweep notes: BK64 helps a lot (longer inner pipeline). BK128 too shallow at 2 stages (91). 64x32 warp (2blk) caps ~142 < 64x64 warp (1blk) 158. More stages (5) didn't help. Decoupled-barrier 128-thread configs (143) < CFG11.
+  - CFG11 stalls: wait 3.77 (mma latency, unhidden at 8 warps/SM), math_pipe 2.15, lg_throttle 1.14.
+
+**Ceiling of fp32-accum interleaved kernel ~158 = 51% peak.** 64x64 warp = 128 fp32 accum regs pins 1 blk/SM.
+
+- v10 fp16-accumulate (m16n8k16.f16x4, 2 accum regs/tile, vectorized 32-bit epilogue). CFG11 = **175 TFLOPS, tensor util 73.9%** but **error UNSTABLE: 0.018/0.018/0.031 across seeds** — occasionally exceeds 0.02. fp16-accum REJECTED as primary (seed-sensitive relative error when GT small).
+
+**DECISION: fp32-accum is primary (stable, accurate).** Best = **v9 CFG11 = 158 TFLOPS, error 3e-5.** fp16-accum v10 kept as experimental only.
+
+**Converged ceiling analysis:** 64x64 warp tile = best (intensity > occupancy). On A100 it's HARD-LIMITED to ~8 warps/SM (1 block): fp32 128 accum regs + smem 159KB both pin 1 block. 64x32 warp (2blk) loses (142<158). Bigger warp 128x64 (4 warps) loses (144). Decoupled 2-block 128-thread (CFG16, BK32) loses (143, smaller block). Deep pipeline (8 stage) loses (117). BK64/3stage is the sweet spot. Tensor util ceiling ~67% fp32 / 74% fp16 at 8 warps/SM. Remaining loss = per-tile barrier bubble + inter-ki mma wait, unhideable at 8 warps/SM.
+
+- v11 = clean dedicated fp32 best (hardcoded 256x128x64 warp64x64 3stage interleaved). split-prefetch tried = 155 (slightly worse, reverted). Clean = **157.4 stable**.
+- v12 = v11 + threadblock swizzle (L2). No change (157.3) — confirms NOT memory bound (DRAM 17%).
+
+**DEFINITIVE diagnosis (v9 CFG11):** issue_active only 16%, tensor pipe active 67%, ALU 4.8% LSU 3% — pure LATENCY-BOUND at 8 warps/SM (1 blk). The ~33% tensor-idle = per-tile barrier bubble (ldmatrix(ki=0) after __syncthreads, ~22cyc, synchronized across all 8 warps -> scheduler idle) + inter-ki mma wait. 64x64 warp is HARD-pinned to 1 blk/SM (128 fp32 accum regs + 159KB smem). Plus ~5% wave-quant tail (512 blk / 108 SM = 4.74 waves; unavoidable for these tile dims).
+
+**CURRENT BEST (stable, primary): v11 / v9-CFG11 fp32 = 158 TFLOPS, err 3e-5 (51% of 312 peak).**
+**v10-CFG11 fp16-accum = 175 TFLOPS but err 0.015-0.021 (borderline, exceeds 0.02 some seeds) — NOT reliable.**
+
+Identified next frontier (high risk): mbarrier async pipeline to desync the per-tile barrier bubble across warps (only path to ~174 fp32 w/ accuracy). cuda::pipeline likely no better than hand cp.async. Bigger BK blocked by smem. 16 warps/SM impossible for 64x64 warp on A100.
+
+**EXHAUSTED (all measured, none beat 158 fp32):**
+- mbarrier raw PTX: `mbarrier.try_wait.parity` is sm_90 ONLY — Ampere needs token-based test_wait which doesn't compose with cross-warp cp.async producer/consumer except via collective cuda::pipeline (keeps bubble). Bubble NOT practically removable on Ampere.
+- fine-grained ldmatrix/mma interleave (1 ldm per 4 mma): 144 — WORSE (ptxas schedules the burst-then-mma better itself).
+- remove `volatile` from mma: neutral (158).
+- threadblock/L2 swizzle: neutral (157, not mem-bound).
+- split global prefetch across ki: 155 (worse).
+- mma loop order ni-outer vs mi-outer: neutral.
+- deep pipeline {128,128,64,4stage}=123, {256,128,32,4stage}=146: both < 158.
+
+**FINAL: fp32 158 TFLOPS (51% peak) is the structural ceiling of a hand-written single-block-per-SM mma kernel on A100.** Gap to CUTLASS ~80% = scheduling sophistication (ptxas can't match hand-tuned SASS) + the unhideable 8-warp/SM latency bubble. Deliverables: v11 (fp32 primary, stable), v10 (fp16-accum 175, borderline accuracy), v9 (configurable sweep, pinned CFG11).
